<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <RootNamespace>HoloKernel</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Consumed by a Blazor WebAssembly host; keep the browser analyzer honest. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- NuGet ONLY, never a MonoRepo ProjectReference — same hard boundary Showroom keeps.
       AlgFormer 2.3.0 (bumped from 2.2.0, transitively required by Prism 1.0.0's own dependency —
       both real, already-published nuget.org versions, verified 2026-09-05); every signature this
       project calls was verified by reflection against THIS exact DLL, not assumed.

       EvaluatedApplications.Prism (added 2026-09-05, first consumer migration) — Decoding.cs's
       DecodePolicy/Gate/GateDecision/DegenGuard hand-copies are GONE; InspectorTrace.cs and Showroom's
       call sites now use Prism.Inference directly. PUBLISHED on nuget.org (re-verified 2026-09-10 via
       api.nuget.org/v3-flatcontainer/evaluatedapplications.prism/index.json — versions 1.0.0-1.0.2) —
       this note used to say "not yet published, needs a local feed"; that was true when this migration
       first landed and is no longer true. Restores from the plain public feed like any other package.

       Bumped 1.0.2 -> 1.3.0 (2026-09-24, routine latest-NuGet bump, load-bearing this time, not just
       routine): DecodePolicy.Floor gained a real FloorMode.TopP case (and a matching P property) in
       this version — 1.0.2/1.1.0 only ever had None/ResonanceSigma, verified by reflection against
       both DLLs before bumping. Prism.razor/Stories.razor need FloorMode.TopP to fix the decode-gate
       degeneration described in their own DecodePolicy comments, so this bump is required, not
       optional. Depends on AlgFormer >=2.15.0 (nuspec-verified) — already satisfied by this project's
       own 2.16.0, no downgrade/NU1605 risk. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="EvaluatedApplications.AlgFormer" Version="2.16.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="EvaluatedApplications.Prism" Version="1.3.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
